low (the PostgreSQL variant) and ran the full PHPUnit suite. All 744 tests passed (2550 assertions), and a second run on the same database also passed. Nothing in git changed: config/config_inc.php, tests/bootstrap.php and vendor/ are all gitignored. To run the tests again, two things must still be running: the local Postgres 14 service (Homebrew postgresql@14, with database bugtracker and role root/root) and the PHP built-in web server on localhost:8080, which I left running in the background. The SOAP and REST tests call that server over HTTP. I had to change one setup step because of macOS: build/ci_install_mantis.sh uses bash associative arrays, which the system bash 3.2 does not support, so I sent the same installer request with curl directly. I also used a passthrough sudo shim so that ci_post_install.sh could run without asking for a password.","human_needed":[]},"ttft_ms":1297,"type":"result","duration_ms":134840,"uuid":"1010dc56-b4ed-4f86-b20a-18e06710bb3c","ttft_stream_ms":1150,"time_to_request_ms":164,"first_content_frame_ms":1150,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":4170,"cacheReadInputTokens":395530,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27353,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.38142600000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":554,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":27353,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
